ArcLibre Alarm disc
===================

This disc holds !Alarm, the original Acorn alarm clock and diary
application. In RISC OS 3.11 it was in the ROM; ArcLibre ships it on this
disc so that the ROM has room for the Econet networking modules.

Running Alarm
-------------

Open this disc's directory viewer and double-click !Alarm. Its clock
appears on the icon bar; click Select on it to set an alarm, and Menu for
its options. Copy !Alarm to a hard disc or another floppy to keep it with
your own applications. Double-clicking a saved alarms file (type Alarms,
&AE9) starts Alarm with those alarms once the Filer has seen !Alarm.

Alarm needs 96K of application memory.

